(1, 'student', 179, 'chat', 'Explain what is database management system in simple English.', 'Hello M R Mohamed Aabid,\n\nLet\'s explain what a Database Management System (DBMS) is in simple English.\n\nImagine you have a lot of information, like all the student names, their grades, and their contact numbers at Eden Campus.\n\n1.  **What is a Database?**\n    *   It\'s like a big, organized collection of all this information. Think of it like a very smart, digital filing cabinet where everything has its own place.\n    *   *Example:* A list of all your friends\' phone numbers is a small database.\n\n2.  **What is a Database Management System (DBMS)?**\n    *   A DBMS is a **special computer program (software)** that helps you manage this big collection of information (the database).\n    *   It\'s like having a very efficient assistant for your digital filing cabinet.\n\n**What does this \"assistant\" (the DBMS) do?**\n\nThe DBMS helps you to:\n\n*   **Create** new databases. (Like setting up a new filing cabinet.)\n*   **Store** information. (Putting new files into the cabinet.)\n*   **Organize** information so it\'s easy to find. (Making sure files are in the right folders.)\n*   **Find** specific information very quickly. (Quickly finding a student\'s grade.)\n*   **Update** information. (Changing a student\'s address if they move.)\n*   **Delete** old or unnecessary information. (Removing a student\'s record if they leave the campus.)\n*   **Keep it safe and secure.** (Making sure only authorized people can see or change certain files.)\n*   **Make backups** so you don\'t lose information.\n\n**Think of it this way:**\n\n*   **Database:** A library full of books (information).\n*   **DBMS:** The librarian and the library\'s computer system. They help you find books, check them out, return them, and keep the library organized and secure.\n\n**Why is it useful?**\n\nA DBMS makes it much easier, faster, and safer to handle large amounts of information. Without it, managing data would be very messy and difficult!\n\nIn short, a **Database Management System (DBMS)** is the software that lets you create, manage, and use a database effectively.\n\n*   **???? ????? ???????? ??????? (DBMS)** ??? ???? ??????? (information collection) ???????? ????????? ???? ?? ?????? ?????? ?????? ?? ?????? ?????????.', 102, 551, '2026-05-19 04:10:03'),
(2, 'student', 179, 'pdf', 'PDF Upload: Cybersecurity and Network Engineering.pdf\nQuestion: can you explain', 'Hello M R Mohamed Aabid! I can help you understand the content of this PDF about Cybersecurity and Network Engineering.\n\nLet\'s go through it page by page.\n\n---\n\n### Page 1: Cybersecurity and Network Engineering (Title Page)\n\nThis page is the title page. It shows that the lesson is about \"Cybersecurity and Network Engineering.\"\n\nThe image on this page gives a quick overview of what cybersecurity involves. It shows different tools and methods used to keep computer systems safe:\n*   **Firewalls:** These are like security guards that control what data can enter or leave a network.\n*   **Intrusion Detection Systems (IDS):** These systems watch for suspicious activity and alert you if someone tries to break in.\n*   **Antivirus Software:** This software helps protect your computer from harmful programs like viruses.\n*   **Security Policies:** These are rules that people must follow to keep the network safe.\n*   **Secure Communications:** This means making sure that messages and data sent over a network cannot be easily read by others.\n*   **Data Loss Prevention:** Tools and methods to stop important data from being lost or stolen.\n*   **Encryption:** This is like scrambling data so that only authorized people can read it. (???? ??????? ?????)\n\n---\n\n### Page 2: What is a Computer Network?\n\nThis page defines what a computer network is:\n*   **Definition:** A computer network is a system where many computers and other devices (like printers) are connected together. They can be connected using wires (wired) or without wires (wireless).\n*   **Purpose:** The main reason for having a network is to **share resources**.\n    *   **Resources** can be things like:\n        *   **Hardware:** For example, multiple computers can use one printer.\n        *   **Software applications:** Programs can be shared across different computers.\n        *   **Data and information:** Files and information can be easily shared between connected devices.\n\nThe image shows two computers connected through a \"Communication Medium\" (like a cable or Wi-Fi), which allows them to share information.\n\n---\n\n### Page 3: Advantages of Networking\n\nThis page lists the main benefits of using a computer network:\n*   Easy Sharing of Resources\n*   Better Communication\n*   Centralized Data Storage\n*   Improved Security\n\n---\n\n### Page 4: Easy Sharing of Resources & Better Communication\n\nThis page explains the first two advantages in more detail:\n\n1.  **Easy Sharing of Resources:**\n    *   When computers are connected, you can easily share things.\n    *   **Example:** In an office, all computers can use one printer instead of needing a separate printer for each computer. You can also share files and internet connections easily.\n\n2.  **Better Communication:**\n    *   Networking makes it easy and fast for people to communicate.\n    *   You can send emails, chat messages, or make video calls very quickly.\n    *   This is useful in offices, schools, and even at home.\n\n---\n\n### Page 5: Centralized Data Storage & Improved Security\n\nThis page explains the next two advantages:\n\n1.  **Centralized Data Storage:**\n    *   Instead of saving files on each computer separately, you can save them in one main place. This main place is often called a **server**. (?????? ????)\n    *   This makes it easier to:\n        *   **Manage data:** Keep track of all files.\n        *   **Back up data:** Make copies of important files easily.\n        *   **Protect data:** Keep files safe.\n\n2.  **Improved Security:**\n    *   In a network, it\'s easier to control who can see or use specific data.\n    *   You can set **permissions** (who can access what), use **passwords**, and take other steps to keep important information safe from people who shouldn\'t see it (unauthorized access).\n\n---\n\n### Page 6: Disadvantages of Networking\n\nThis page lists the main problems or drawbacks of using a computer network:\n*   Virus and Malware Spread Quickly\n*   High Setup and Maintenance Cost\n*   Security Problems\n*   Server Failure Affects All\n\n---\n\n### Page 7: Virus and Malware Spread Quickly & High Setup and Maintenance Cost\n\nThis page explains the first two disadvantages:\n\n1.  **Virus and Malware Spread Quickly:**\n    *   If one computer in a network gets a virus or other harmful software (malware), it can easily spread to all other connected computers.\n    *   This can damage files and affect the entire system.\n\n2.  **High Setup and Maintenance Cost:**\n    *   Building a network needs special equipment like **switches**, **routers**, and **cables**. These can be expensive.\n    *   Also, you might need to pay for ongoing maintenance and repairs to keep the network running smoothly.\n\n---\n\n### Page 8: Security Problems & Server Failure Affects All\n\nThis page explains the next two disadvantages:\n\n1.  **Security Problems:**\n    *   If the network\'s security is not strong enough, hackers (people who try to break into systems) can get into the network and steal important data.\n    *   You need extra security measures like strong passwords and **firewalls** (like the ones mentioned on page 1) to keep the network safe.\n\n2.  **Server Failure Affects All:**\n    *   In many networks, there\'s a main computer called a **server** (as mentioned on page 5).\n    *   If this server stops working, all the other computers connected to it might lose access to their files and services. This can cause a lot of problems.\n\n---\n\n### Page 9: Types of Networks\n\nThis page introduces different types of networks. Networks are groups of connected computers that share data and resources. They can be grouped by their size, the distance they cover, or how they are connected.\n\nHere are the types listed:\n*   **Local Area Network (LAN):** For a small area.\n*   **Wide Area Network (WAN):** For a very large area.\n*   **Metropolitan Area Network (MAN):** For a city-sized area.\n*   **Personal Area Network (PAN):** For a very small personal area.\n*   **Wireless Networks (WLAN):** Networks that use Wi-Fi.\n*   **Virtual Private Network (VPN):** A secure connection over a public network.\n\nThe image shows how LANs, MANs, and WANs cover different geographical sizes.\n\n---\n\n### Page 10: Local Area Network (LAN)\n\nThis page explains a **Local Area Network (LAN)**:\n*   **What it is:** A LAN covers a small area, like a home, an office, or a school. (???? ?????????? ???? ?? ??????)\n*   **Connection:** Computers in a LAN are connected closely, usually within one building.\n*   **Speed:** They have a fast connection speed.\n*   **Example:** Computers in an office connected to the same printer.\n\nThe image shows several computers and a server connected together, representing a typical LAN setup.\n\n---\n\n### Page 11: Metropolitan Area Network (MAN)\n\nThis page explains a **Metropolitan Area Network (MAN)**:\n*   **What it is:** A MAN covers a larger area than a LAN, typically spanning across a city or a large campus. (?????? ???? ????? ?????????? ????? ??? ??????)\n*   It connects multiple LANs together within that area.\n*   **Examples:**\n    *   A city government connecting all its offices in different parts of the city.\n    *   University campuses spread across a city.\n    *   Cable TV networks in a metropolitan area.\n\nThe image shows several LANs (represented by buildings) connected together to form a MAN.\n\n---\n\n### Page 12: Wide Area Network (WAN)\n\nThis page explains a **Wide Area Network (WAN)**:\n*   **What it is:** A WAN is a computer network that connects computers and networks over a very large geographical area. (????? ??????? ?????????? ????? ??? ??????)\n*   **Coverage:** It can connect different cities, countries, or even entire continents.\n*   **Example:** The internet is the largest WAN.\n\nThe image shows computers connected across the globe, illustrating the vast reach of a WAN.\n\n---\n\n### Page 13: Types of Networks (Based on connection)\n\nThis page shows another way to classify networks: based on how devices are connected and interact.\nThe three main types are:\n*   **Peer-to-Peer network**\n*   **Client-Server network**\n*   **Hybrid network**\n\n---', 13009, 1890, '2026-05-19 04:15:27'),
(3, 'student', 179, 'chat', 'Explain what is database management system in simple English.', 'Hello M R Mohamed Aabid,\n\nA **Database Management System (DBMS)** is like a special computer program that helps you manage a lot of information in an organized way.\n\nLet\'s break it down:\n\n1.  **Database:** Imagine a very organized digital filing cabinet. This cabinet holds all your information (like student names, marks, addresses, etc.) in a structured way.\n2.  **Management System:** This is the software that acts like the \"librarian\" or \"manager\" for your filing cabinet.\n\nSo, a **DBMS** is the software that allows you to:\n\n*   **Create** new databases (like setting up a new filing cabinet).\n*   **Store** information safely (putting files into the cabinet).\n*   **Organize** information so it\'s easy to find (labeling folders, putting them in alphabetical order).\n*   **Retrieve** information quickly (finding a specific student\'s marks).\n*   **Update** information (changing a student\'s address).\n*   **Delete** information (removing old records).\n\n**Think of it this way:**\n\n*   If you have a list of all your friends\' phone numbers on a piece of paper, that\'s like a simple database.\n*   If you use a special app on your phone to store, search, and update those numbers easily, that app is acting like a simple DBMS.\n\n**Why is it useful?**\n\nIt makes it very easy to handle large amounts of data, keep it safe, make sure it\'s correct, and find what you need quickly.\n\nIn simple Sinhala, a DBMS is a **???? ????? ???????? ???????** (Datta Samuda Kalamanakarana Paddhatiya) – a system to manage your data.', 102, 381, '2026-05-19 04:18:19'),
(4, 'student', 179, 'chat', 'you know the eden campus', 'Yes, I do!\n\nI am the Eden Campus ELMS AI Assistant. My purpose is to help students like you with your studies and provide support for your courses here at Eden Campus.\n\nHow can I help you today, M R Mohamed Aabid?', 97, 53, '2026-05-19 04:20:09'),
(5, 'student', 179, 'chat', 'oyata monawage dewal tha karanna pulwan', 'M R Mohamed Aabid, oyage prashnaya hondai! (That\'s a good question!)\n\nMama Eden Campus ELMS AI Assistant kenek. Oyata oyage paadam walata udaw karanna mama innawa. Mama karana dewal mehemai:\n\n1.  **Vishaya Karunu Pahasuwen Pahadili Karanawa** (Explain concepts easily): Oyatathurunu therenne nathi deyak thiyenawanam, eka pahasuwen pahadili karanna puluwan.\n    *   *Example:* \"What is photosynthesis?\" (Photosynthesis kiyanne mokadda?)\n\n2.  **Udaharan Denawa** (Give examples): Vishaya karunu hondin therenna udaharan denna puluwan.\n    *   *Example:* \"Can you give me an example of a good thesis statement?\" (Hondha thesis statement ekakata udaharanayak denna puluwanda?)\n\n3.  **Assignment Walata Udaw Karanawa** (Help with assignments):\n    *   **Outline Hadanna** (Create outlines): Oya assignment ekakata plan ekak hadanna udaw karanna puluwan.\n    *   **Checklists Denawa** (Provide checklists): Oya assignment eka sampurna karanna ona dewal check karanna list ekak denna puluwan.\n    *   **Grammar Hadanna** (Improve grammar): Oyage liweem wala waradi hadanna udaw karanna puluwan.\n    *   **Marking Criteria Pahadili Karanawa** (Explain marking criteria): Assignment ekata lakuunu labena hati pahadili karanna puluwan.\n    *   **NOTE:** Mama oyage assignment eka oyata liyala denne nehe. Oyata igena ganna udaw karanawa vitharai.\n\n4.  **Paadam Prashna Walata Pilituru Denawa** (Answer study questions): Oyage paadam walata adala prashna walata pilituru denna puluwan.\n\n**Mama Nokarana Deval** (Things I cannot do):\n\n*   **Cheating, Plagiarism Walata Udaw Karanna Behe** (Cannot help with cheating or plagiarism): Mama oyata waradi widiyata liyanna, copy karanna udaw karanne nehe.\n*   **Assessments Walata Waradi Vidiyata Udaw Karanna Behe** (Cannot help bypass assessments dishonestly): Oyage parikshana walata nikanma pilituru denna behe.\n*   **Oyage Final Submissions Liyanna Behe** (Cannot write your final submissions): Graded assignments walata mama oyata pilituru liyala denne nehe.\n\nMama oyata hondin, surakshithawa igena ganna udaw karanna innawa.\n\nM R Mohamed Aabid, oyata udaw karanna puluwan prashnayak thiyenawanam ahanna!', 104, 636, '2026-05-19 06:23:11'),
(6, 'student', 179, 'tutor', 'oyata monawage dewal tha karanna pulwan', 'Hi M R Mohamed Aabid! I\'m your ELMS AI Assistant. I\'m here to help you with your studies at Eden Campus.\n\nHere are some things I can do for you:\n\n1.  **Explain difficult topics:** If you don\'t understand something in your lessons, I can explain it in simple words. (????? ????? ???????? ????? ???????.)\n2.  **Help with assignments:** I can help you understand assignment questions, create outlines, and check your grammar. (???? ??? ??? ???? ????? ???????.)\n3.  **Improve your writing:** I can help you make your English writing better and clearer. (??? ????????? ????? ?????? ????? ???????.)\n4.  **Guide you with marking criteria:** I can help you understand what your teachers are looking for in your assignments. (????? ??? ????? ?????? ???? ???? ????? ???????.)\n5.  **Give practice questions:** I can give you small practice questions to test your understanding. (?????? ??????? ????? ???????.)\n\n**What I cannot do:**\n\n*   I cannot do your assignments for you.\n*   I cannot help you cheat or plagiarize.\n*   I cannot write your final submissions.\n\nMy goal is to help you learn and understand, so you can do your best work!\n\nDo you have a specific topic you\'d like help with right now?', 121, 324, '2026-05-19 06:26:05'),
(7, 'student', 179, 'tutor', 'mata english walin wachana 5 k liyanna oni', 'Hi M R Mohamed Aabid! I can help you with that.\n(??? ???? ????? ???????.)\n\nYou want to write 5 words in English. Here are some very simple words:\n\n1.  **Cat** (??????) - This is an animal.\n2.  **Dog** (???????) - This is another animal.\n3.  **Book** (?????) - You read this.\n4.  **Pen** (?????) - You write with this.\n5.  **Apple** (???? ???????) - This is a fruit.\n\nDo you want to learn more about these words, or do you want words for a different topic?\n(??? ?? ??? ??? ?? ??????? ????, ??????? ??? ????????? ??? ??? ?????)\n\n---\n**Practice Question:**\nCan you tell me one more animal word in English? (????????????? ???? ??????? ???? ?????? ?????????)', 122, 243, '2026-05-19 06:27:08'),
(8, 'student', 179, 'tutor', 'ungalukku tamil la solla eluma', 'Yes, I can understand and respond in Tamil! (???, ??????? ??????? ????????????????? ????????????? ????????!)\n\nHowever, my main instructions are to use **simple English** for our conversations. I will add brief Sinhala explanations only when it\'s very helpful.\n\nBut if you need to ask something in Tamil, please do! I will understand.\n\nSo, let\'s try to use simple English mostly, okay?', 118, 90, '2026-05-19 06:27:57'),
(9, 'student', 179, 'chat', 'What is Software?', 'Hello M R Mohamed Aabid,\n\nSoftware is like the \"brain\" or the \"instructions\" for a computer.\n\nHere\'s a simple way to understand it:\n\n1.  **It\'s a Set of Instructions:** Software is a collection of programs, data, and instructions that tell a computer what to do and how to do it.\n    *   Think of it like a recipe. The recipe (software) tells you step-by-step how to cook a meal. Without the recipe, you wouldn\'t know what to do with the ingredients.\n\n2.  **It\'s Not Physical:** You cannot touch software. It exists digitally. This is different from **hardware**, which are the physical parts of a computer you *can* touch (like the screen, keyboard, mouse, or the computer\'s internal parts).\n\n3.  **What it Does:** Software makes computers useful! Without software, a computer is just a collection of metal and plastic. Software allows you to:\n    *   Browse the internet\n    *   Write documents\n    *   Play games\n    *   Watch videos\n    *   And much more!\n\n**Two Main Types of Software:**\n\n*   **System Software:** This helps the computer run itself.\n    *   **Example:** Your computer\'s **Operating System** (like Windows, macOS, Android, or iOS). It manages all the hardware and other software.\n\n*   **Application Software:** This helps *you* do specific tasks.\n    *   **Examples:** Web browsers (like Chrome or Firefox), word processors (like Microsoft Word), games, social media apps (like Facebook or Instagram), video players.\n\n**In simple terms:** Software is the invisible part of a computer that gives it life and tells it what to do.\n\n*(???? ???????, ???????? (Software) ??? ????????? ????? ?? ????? ?? ???? ?? ????? ???? ???? ?????? ???????. ?? ??? ?????? ?? ?????? ??????? ?????.)*', 96, 447, '2026-05-19 06:31:13'),
(10, 'student', 179, 'chat', 'hello', 'Hello M R Mohamed Aabid! I am your ELMS AI Assistant.\n\nHow can I help you with your studies today? ?', 93, 28, '2026-05-19 06:55:37'),
(11, 'student', 179, 'chat', 'webdesign', 'Hello M R Mohamed Aabid!\n\n\"Web design\" is a very interesting and broad topic!\n\nIn simple terms, **web design** is about planning, creating, and maintaining websites. It involves how a website looks (the visual part) and how it works (the functional part).\n\nTo help you best, could you tell me what specific part of web design you\'re interested in? For example, are you curious about:\n\n*   **What it is?** (I just gave a brief answer!)\n*   **What skills are needed?**\n*   **The different stages of designing a website?**\n*   **Specific tools or software?**\n*   **How to make a website look good?**\n*   **How to make a website easy to use?**\n\nLet me know what you\'d like to explore!', 94, 179, '2026-05-19 06:56:00'),
(12, 'student', 179, 'chat', 'create web site', 'Hello M R Mohamed Aabid,\n\nCreating a website is a great goal! There are different ways to do it, depending on how much control you want and how much you want to learn.\n\nHere are the main ways to create a website, explained simply:\n\n### 1. Using a Website Builder (Easiest for Beginners)\n\n*   **What it is:** These are online platforms that let you build a website without writing any code. You can drag and drop elements like text, pictures, and buttons onto your page.\n*   **Good for:** People who want a website quickly and easily, without learning technical skills.\n*   **Examples:** Wix, Squarespace, Shopify (for online stores).\n*   **How it works:** You choose a template (a pre-designed layout), then customize it with your own content.\n\n### 2. Using a Content Management System (CMS) like WordPress\n\n*   **What it is:** A CMS is software that helps you manage your website\'s content easily. WordPress is the most popular one. It\'s more flexible than a website builder but still doesn\'t always require coding.\n*   **Good for:** Blogs, business websites, and sites that need more features than a simple builder offers.\n*   **How it works:** You install WordPress (often with one click from your web host), choose a theme (design), and add plugins (extra features) to build your site.\n\n### 3. Coding It Yourself (Most Control, but Harder)\n\n*   **What it is:** This means writing all the code for your website from scratch using languages like HTML (for content structure), CSS (for design and style), and JavaScript (for interactive features).\n*   **Good for:** People who want full control over every detail, or who want to become web developers.\n*   **How it works:** You write the code in a text editor, then upload it to a web server.\n\n---\n\n### What You Will Need for Any Website:\n\n1.  **Domain Name:** This is your website\'s address on the internet (e.g., `yourwebsite.com`). (???? ?????? ??????)\n2.  **Web Hosting:** This is where your website\'s files are stored so people can access them online. Think of it as the \"home\" for your website. (???? ????? ???? ??? ??????)\n3.  **Content:** Your text, images, videos, and other information you want to share.\n\n---\n\nTo help me guide you better, could you tell me a little more about what you want to create?\n\n*   **What kind of website do you want to make?** (e.g., a blog, an online store, a portfolio to show your work, a website for a business, a personal page?)\n*   **Do you have any experience with coding or building websites?**\n*   **What is your main goal for this website?**\n\nOnce I know more, I can give you more specific advice!', 95, 646, '2026-05-19 06:56:37'),
(13, 'student', 179, 'chat', 'Hello', 'Hello M R Mohamed Aabid!\n\nI\'m your ELMS AI Assistant. How can I help you with your studies today?\n\nRemember, I\'m here to help you understand topics, plan your work, and improve your writing, but I cannot help with cheating or dishonest work.', 108, 60, '2026-05-19 06:58:57'),
(14, 'student', 179, 'chat', 'What is the new Ai tools a there', 'It\'s great you\'re curious about new AI tools! The world of Artificial Intelligence (AI) is growing very fast, and new tools appear all the time.\n\nHere are some main types of new AI tools you might hear about, with examples:\n\n1.  **Language AI (Large Language Models - LLMs):**\n    *   **What they do:** These AIs can understand and generate human-like text. They can answer questions, write essays (but remember our rules about original work!), summarize information, brainstorm ideas, and even translate languages.\n    *   **Examples:** ChatGPT, Google Gemini, Claude, Microsoft Copilot.\n    *   *Sinhala:* ???? AI (Bhasha AI) - ????? ???????? ??? ??? ?????, ?????? ???????.\n\n2.  **Image and Art AI:**\n    *   **What they do:** These AIs can create images, drawings, and art from text descriptions (prompts). You can tell them what you want to see, and they will generate it.\n    *   **Examples:** Midjourney, DALL-E, Stable Diffusion.\n    *   *Sinhala:* ???/??? AI (Rupa/Kala AI) - ????? ?? ???? ??? ???? ??????? ????? ???????.\n\n3.  **Coding and Development AI:**\n    *   **What they do:** These tools help programmers write code faster, find errors, and suggest improvements.\n    *   **Examples:** GitHub Copilot.\n    *   *Sinhala:* ?????? AI (Kethakarana AI) - ?????? ??? ?????? ???? ?????.\n\n4.  **Productivity and Organization AI:**\n    *   **What they do:** These AIs are built into other software to help you work smarter. They can summarize documents, create presentations, help with data analysis, or manage your schedule.\n    *   **Examples:** AI features in Microsoft 365 (like Copilot in Word, Excel, PowerPoint), Notion AI.\n    *   *Sinhala:* ???????? AI (Paladaitha AI) - ??? ??? ???? ?????, ???????? ????? ???? ?????.\n\n5.  **Research and Learning AI:**\n    *   **What they do:** These tools can help you find information, summarize academic papers, create study guides, and get quick answers with sources.\n    *   **Examples:** Perplexity AI, Elicit.\n    *   *Sinhala:* ???????/??????? AI (Parishana/Igenum AI) - ??????? ??????, ???? ???? ???? ?????.\n\n**Important Reminder:**\nWhile these tools are powerful, always remember to use them responsibly. Do not use AI for cheating, plagiarism, or to bypass assessments. Your learning and original work are very important for your success.\n\nDo you want to know more about any specific type of AI tool?', 115, 655, '2026-05-19 06:59:57'),
(15, 'student', 179, 'chat', 'Lesson questions', 'Hello! I can help you with your lesson questions.\n\nPlease tell me:\n1.  **Which lesson** are your questions about? (e.g., Biology, History, Math, English)\n2.  **What are the questions?** (You can type them out or tell me the topic.)\n\nOnce I have more information, I can help you understand concepts, explain examples, or guide you on how to answer them.\n\nRemember, I cannot help with cheating or giving you direct answers for graded assignments. I can help you learn and understand the material better.', 109, 119, '2026-05-19 07:17:04'),
(16, 'student', 179, 'chat', 'history', 'Hello! \"History\" is a very big and interesting subject.\n\nTo help you best, could you please tell me what you would like to know about history? For example, are you interested in:\n\n*   A specific time period (like Ancient Egypt, World War II)?\n*   A particular region or country (like Sri Lankan history, European history)?\n*   A certain topic within history (like the history of science, social history)?\n*   Help with a history assignment or essay?\n*   Tips for studying history?\n\nOnce you tell me more, I can give you a more helpful answer!', 108, 127, '2026-05-19 07:17:31'),
